three beloved grand theft auto games  have been re-released as part of the  definitive edition the visuals and  controls of gta 3 vice city and san  andreas have been updated and upgraded  and getting three classic games for one  makes this package a pretty sweet deal  sadly these remasters are currently  suffering from glitches audio problems  and a mess of strange visuals so here's  our list of six things that rockstar and  grove street games need to fix if you  like gta or video games in general  remember to subscribe to gamespot for  more let's begin  the original grand theft auto 3 opens  with a police van traveling through a  rainy liberty city before being attacked  it's your first look at the game's open  world and it really sets the mood the  definitive version does the same but oh  my god that rain what is happening what  was once a subtle drizzle over the  screen is now an assault to the eyes  it's not just that it looks worse than  the original but it makes visibility  extremely unclear this issue affects all  three games but it hits gta 3 the  hardest as it rains in liberty city  quite frequently of all the strange  graphical glitches in this collection  this one we would love to see fix the  most  aiming at your targets is sometimes more  trouble than it's worth in gun heavy  battles against multiple enemies  targeting tends to lock onto the wrong  person usually of the unarmed variety  this gta 5 and san andreas hybrid style  of aiming works when there are 3-5  enemies but if you're surrounded which  happens a ton you're at the disadvantage  no matter which gun you have there is a  quote classic style of aiming available  in the game's menu but it's not nearly  as fast or precise at snapping multiple  targets nor does it have the color-coded  health like before surviving gunfights  in the original ps2 version comes easier  as a result  the character models we've all seen them  fortunately the main group of characters  seems to have gotten away unscathed but  everyone else in the definitive version  is looking rough some models like cj's  first girlfriend denise look like  completely different people some are  downright terrifying many lack any  facial details and share the same creepy  eyeballs  [Music]  gta's longer multi-step missions feature  some crucial steps to help get things  done the definitive edition currently  lacks most of these leaving players with  long unskippable moments with no context  when the time comes to begin the mission  new and even returning players will be  met with little to no follow-up  instructions in our play time this issue  occurred in gta san andreas four times  at least we're happy to report that the  breach tab in the menu can finally come  in handy for a quick catch-up but let's  be real this information should not be  missing  at launch gta's definitive edition has  some noticeably harsh audio problems the  most prominent one we found is the  sinking of cutscene dialogue or the lack  of sync  and you'll see how we try out subtle  things without recourse to  unnecessary violence  all right i'll ride with you  other issues include music track  skipping almost as if cj were actually  listening to a cd  also during cut scenes just before  fading to black dialogue can get  abruptly cut  let's go [ __ ]  this new york look like it's up to us  we shall fight to the  this category is a catch-all of all the  little things that seem to have slipped  through the cracks we'd love to hear  yours in the comments but here are some  we've found  transparency effects haven't held up too  well this includes everything from car  fires to ryder's blunt smoke to smoke  grenades barely functioning  what the why isn't t-bone dying he's a  bullet sponge  i rose up to hitman level already with  my pistol why won't you die  other noticeable bugs include tommy  versetti's glitchy crouch animation when  firing a weapon missing or invisible  assets like this bridge shaky license  plate graphics that pop in and out  hairstyles like this high fade not even  working unless we forget about the  constant lag on the nintendo switch  version especially while docked this is  what a building exploding looks like  uncut  there are also some updates to the  lighting and color effect which take  away some of the magic when it comes to  grand theft auto san andreas  specifically the early 90s vibe was  illustrated perfectly in the original  with its sunny deep orange tint this  well established look for the game has  been dramatically shifted in the  definitive edition where the regular  palette of the city's colors resemble  that more of gta v  even with bloom lens flare and fidelity  mode all turned on the 1990s look of san  andreas hasn't fully been restored  without that southern california orange  glaze we come to expect  anybody in the world  it's hard to complain about a trilogy of  games that have brought us years of joy  these aren't terrible or even bad  remasters but if rockstar wants to use  the term definitive we hope these issues  and more can be addressed so that  players can enjoy these games for more  years to come let us know what else you  think should be fixed in the comments  drop a like if you enjoyed the video and  as always thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

